  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: AppRC 3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'After a new cancer treatment is approved, your hospital participates
    in a national registry to track how patients are doing on this treatment over
    time. You help collect reports from patients and physicians and submit this information
    to the registry.


    <b>How does a research coordinator support ongoing research
    for newly approved treatments?</b>'
  explanation: Research coordinators support post-market surveillance by organizing
    records and submitting required reports to the appropriate teams. Clear and accurate
    reporting helps ensure patient experiences are included in ongoing safety monitoring
    and reviewed alongside information from many other patients. This careful documentation
    helps ensure real-world safety information is collected consistently and can
    be reviewed over time.
  correctAnswer: 'By managing and submitting reports so safety information is up
    to date and accurate '
  incorrectAnswer1: By providing medical guidance to patients about how to manage
    side effects
  incorrectAnswer2: By changing how the new treatment is prescribed based on early
    reports
  incorrectAnswer3: By reviewing the reported data and deciding whether the treatment
    should stay on the market
  questionRole: Research Coordinator
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Approval
